      "title": "Accepted Students",
      "description": "Accepted Students - Undergraduate | Lesley University Skip to main content Search Breadcrumb Home Admissions Admissions Accepted Students - Undergr... Main Reach My Education Goals My Education Goals Reach My Education Goals Education Programs Undergraduate Programs Master's Programs PhD Programs Certificate Programs Mental Health & Well Being Programs Undergraduate Programs Master's Programs Counseling & Psychology Expressive Therapies Social Work PhD Programs Certificate Programs Art & Design Programs Undergraduate Programs MFA in Visual and Literary Arts Liberal Arts & Business Programs Undergraduate Programs Graduate Programs Certificate Programs Threshold Programs Life at Lesley Housing Threshold Housing Clubs and Activities Athletics Dining International Student Services (ISS) International F-1 and Form I-20 International Student Housing International Student Forms Travel Information Understanding Your Immigration Documents Maintaining Legal F-1 Status Work Authorization Practical Tips for International Students Student Support Resources Avoid Scams and Frauds Join Admissions Undergraduate Students How to Apply Admissions Visits & Events Accepted Students Submit Your Deposit Graduate Students How to Apply Education Programs Mental Health & Well-Being Programs Art & Design Programs Liberal Arts & Business Admissions Visits & Events Accepted Students Submit Your Deposit Transfer Students How to Apply Admissions Visits & Events Accepted Students Submit Your Deposit Mass Guarantee Degree Completion Students How to Apply Admissions Visits & Events Accepted Students Submit Your Deposit International Students How to Apply Admissions Visits & Events Accepted Students Submit Your Deposit Threshold Students How to Apply Admissions Visits & Events Accepted Students Submit Your Deposit Meet the Admissions Team Costs & Financial Aid Options for Financing Your Education Private Scholarships Maine Scholars Program Urban Scholars Initiative Hometown Scholars Camões Scholars Understand the Cost of Attending Lesley Secure Your Funding and Pay Your Bill Student Financial Services Policies My Professional & Life Goals My Professional & Life Goals Reach My Professional & Life Goals Continuing Education Education Mental Health & Well-Being Art & Design Liberal Arts & Business Threshold Programs Professional Networks Priority Job Matching Program Alumni Engagement My Organization's Goals My Organization's Goals Reach My Organization's Goals Recruit Talent Become a Scholar Partner Priority Job Matching Program Retain Talent My Philanthropic Goals My Philanthropic Goals Reach My Philanthropic Goals Support Education at Lesley Support Mental Health & Well-Being Support Art & Design Support Liberal Arts & Business Support Threshold Campus Renovations and Future Vision Emerald Key Society Give Online Explore About Lesley About Lesley Explore About Lesley Leadership Faculty Strategic Framework Scholar Partner Program Fall Weekend 2026 Thought Leadership Series Work at Lesley Equity, Diversity, Inclusion, and Justice Updates from the President News & Stories Events Facility Rentals Contact Internal Internal Internal Academic Meetings and Selected Community Events 2026-2027 Brand Center Services Directory Support Hub Course Catalog myLesley Lesley Experience Portal Policies & Legal Academic Calendar Academic Catalog Institutional Review Board (IRB) MBTA Passes Veteran Benefits & Resources Accepted Students - Undergraduate We’re Glad You’re Here! We are thrilled to welcome you to Lesley. We invite you to explore our campus, meet our faculty and staff, and immerse yourself in everything our community has to offer. Congratulations on your acceptance to Lesley — an amazing adventure awaits. View this flip-book to learn more about getting started at Lesley. Please carefully review this important information for accepted students, and ​ reach out to the admissions team if you have questions. Submit Your Enrollment Contract and Deposit Congratulations and welcome to Lesley! You’ve just made an awesome choice by joining the Lynx community. To lock in your spot in the upcoming class, go ahead and submit this form . Good news: no funds are needed to submit your deposit today! Once you hit submit, one of our friendly admissions counselors will reach out to help you tackle the next steps in your enrollment adventure. Fill Out Your Housing Application (Resident Students Only) Get ready to join us on campus! If you're a Lesley resident student, please submit your housing application to secure on-campus housing today . ​Understand Your Financing Options We’re committed to making a Lesley education attainable and affordable. Our financial aid team will work with you and your family to help you understand what financial aid options are available and put together a plan that meets your needs. Schedule an appointment with a Student Financial Planner Schedule with Christina Griecci Schedule with Tramel Griffith Schedule with Bree Lucas Schedule with Miriam McAvoy Schedule with Audrey Mitchell Schedule with Fallyn Jefferson Schedule with Taylor Rogers For General Information ​​Learn more about cost & financial aid Classroom Visits Classroom Visits Curious about what it’s like to be a student at Lesley University? We’re excited to offer prospective undergraduate students the opportunity to sit in on a college class and experience campus learning firsthand. Register below! We're currently offering classroom visits for the following programs: Education Psychology+ Art & Design Liberal Arts & Business ​Take a Tour and Explore Other Ways to Connect Campus Tour Now that you’ve committed, join us for a campus tour to see for yourself what makes Lesley such a great place to be. If you want to visit on a specific date and time that is not available through the online scheduling system, call us at 617-349-8800 or email admissions@lesley.edu . Sign up for a campus tour Additional Resources Check out these additional resources for other ways to get to know Lesley as you prepare to join us as a new student: Explore our Life at Lesley YouTube Channel ​​See Our Residence Halls ​​Learn About On-Campus Clubs and Activities ​​Explore Athletics ​​​ Center for Student Success and Advising Honors at Lesley Learn more about Honors at an upcoming Virtual Information Session ​Get Ready for Your First Day Here are some important things to know and steps to follow as you begin your journey as a Lesley student and prepare for your first day of classes. Access Your Lesley Email A Lesley email address has been assigned to you, and appears on your Enrollment Confirmation Letter. Once you’re accepted to Lesley, all university emails are sent to you at this address, so be sure to check your account frequently. Your password is the same one you’ve been using to check the status of your documents during the admissions process. If you have not activated your account yet, you can do so by visiting our Password Management site. Set Up Your Electronic Accounts Access your myLesley account This online course portal is where you can access class syllabi, assignments, online discussion boards, and library resources. Access your Self-Service account This is where you can find administrative information regarding your class schedules, grades, financial aid, and more. You will also use Self-Service to register for your courses. Register for courses by logging into your Self-Service account. Connect With Your Academic Advisor If you have any questions about courses or your class schedule, you should reach out to your advisor. Advisor contact information can be found on your Enrollment Confirmation Letter. Or, you can reach out to us at advising@lesley.edu for help. Obtain your ID card and purchase textbooks Lesley ID cards may be obtained at the Doble Public Safety Office at 34 Mellen Street, Cambridge, MA. ID cards are available 24 hours a day, seven days a week. Textbooks are available at the Lesley University Bookstore . Your textbooks can also be delivered to your home, where you can order them online to buy or rent on several websites. If purchasing a textbook is a hardship for you, please speak to your advisor and your professor. You should purchase your textbooks before classes start and no later than the end of the first day of classes. Questions? Contact Our Admissions Team If you have any questions as you work throughout the application process, please reach out to our ​ Admissions Counselors , who can assist you and provide additional information. General phone and email: 617-349-8800 admissions@lesley.edu Take the next step Ready to begin your journey with Lesley? ​Share some basic information by filling out one of the forms below so that we can reach out to you with more information about our programs. Or, email admissions@lesley.edu to connect with a member of our admissions team. Undergraduate & Transfer: Inquiry Form Close | Visit | Apply Graduate: Inquiry Form Close | Visit | Apply Threshold Programs: Inquiry Form Close | Visit | Apply Lesley University Lesley University 29 Everett St, Cambridge, MA, 02138 617-868-9600 | Contact Lesley | Work at Lesley Instagram X LinkedIn Facebook YouTube Lesley is more than a university. We are an education and resource hub that educates and supports the world’s best practitioners in Education, Mental Health & Well-Being, Art & Design, Liberal Arts & Business. Lesley also educates neurodiverse learners through its innovative Threshold Programs. Learn more about Lesley ! Request Info Visit Apply Accessibility Privacy Policy Non-Discrimination Notice Accreditation © 2026 Lesley University"
    },
    "https://lesley.edu/admissions/graduate-students/accepted-students-graduate": {
      "title": "Accepted Students",
      "description": "Accepted Students - Graduate | Lesley University Skip to main content Search Breadcrumb Home Admissions Admissions Accepted Students - Graduate Main Reach My Education Goals My Education Goals Reach My Education Goals Education Programs Undergraduate Programs Master's Programs PhD Programs Certificate Programs Mental Health & Well Being Programs Undergraduate Programs Master's Programs Counseling & Psychology Expressive Therapies Social Work PhD Programs Certificate Programs Art & Design Programs Undergraduate Programs MFA in Visual and Literary Arts Liberal Arts & Business Programs Undergraduate Programs Graduate Programs Certificate Programs Threshold Programs Life at Lesley Housing Threshold Housing Clubs and Activities Athletics Dining International Student Services (ISS) International F-1 and Form I-20 International Student Housing International Student Forms Travel Information Understanding Your Immigration Documents Maintaining Legal F-1 Status Work Authorization Practical Tips for International Students Student Support Resources Avoid Scams and Frauds Join Admissions Undergraduate Students How to Apply Admissions Visits & Events Accepted Students Submit Your Deposit Graduate Students How to Apply Education Programs Mental Health & Well-Being Programs Art & Design Programs Liberal Arts & Business Admissions Visits & Events Accepted Students Submit Your Deposit Transfer Students How to Apply Admissions Visits & Events Accepted Students Submit Your Deposit Mass Guarantee Degree Completion Students How to Apply Admissions Visits & Events Accepted Students Submit Your Deposit International Students How to Apply Admissions Visits & Events Accepted Students Submit Your Deposit Threshold Students How to Apply Admissions Visits & Events Accepted Students Submit Your Deposit Meet the Admissions Team Costs & Financial Aid Options for Financing Your Education Private Scholarships Maine Scholars Program Urban Scholars Initiative Hometown Scholars Camões Scholars Understand the Cost of Attending Lesley Secure Your Funding and Pay Your Bill Student Financial Services Policies My Professional & Life Goals My Professional & Life Goals Reach My Professional & Life Goals Continuing Education Education Mental Health & Well-Being Art & Design Liberal Arts & Business Threshold Programs Professional Networks Priority Job Matching Program Alumni Engagement My Organization's Goals My Organization's Goals Reach My Organization's Goals Recruit Talent Become a Scholar Partner Priority Job Matching Program Retain Talent My Philanthropic Goals My Philanthropic Goals Reach My Philanthropic Goals Support Education at Lesley Support Mental Health & Well-Being Support Art & Design Support Liberal Arts & Business Support Threshold Campus Renovations and Future Vision Emerald Key Society Give Online Explore About Lesley About Lesley Explore About Lesley Leadership Faculty Strategic Framework Scholar Partner Program Fall Weekend 2026 Thought Leadership Series Work at Lesley Equity, Diversity, Inclusion, and Justice Updates from the President News & Stories Events Facility Rentals Contact Internal Internal Internal Academic Meetings and Selected Community Events 2026-2027 Brand Center Services Directory Support Hub Course Catalog myLesley Lesley Experience Portal Policies & Legal Academic Calendar Academic Catalog Institutional Review Board (IRB) MBTA Passes Veteran Benefits & Resources Accepted Students - Graduate Welcome to Your Next Chapter Congratulations, you’re officially part of the Lesley graduate community. We invite you to explore our campus, meet faculty and staff, and immerse yourself in everything our community has to offer. Congratulations on your acceptance to Lesley. Please carefully review this important information for accepted students, and ​reach out to the admissions team if you have questions. Graduate Accepted Student Orientation and Reception For Students Accepted for Fall 2026 –– Virtual Graduate New Student Orientation We invite you to join us for our Virtual Graduate New Student Orientation on August 20, 2026, from 6:00–7:30 PM ET . During this session, you'll learn about valuable campus resources, connect with the Lesley community, and gain important information to help you prepare for the start of the fall semester. We look forward to welcoming you and helping you begin your graduate journey at Lesley. Register for Fall 2026 New Student Orientation Submit Your Enrollment Contract and Deposit Congratulations and welcome to Lesley! You’ve just made an awesome choice by joining the Lynx community. To lock in your spot in the upcoming class, go ahead and submit this form . Good news: no funds are needed to submit your deposit today! Once you hit submit, one of our friendly admissions counselors will reach out to help you tackle the next steps in your enrollment adventure. ​Understand Your Financing Options We’re committed to making a Lesley education attainable and affordable. Our financial aid team will help you understand what financial aid options are available and put together a plan that meets your needs. Learn more about cost and financial aid Getting Ready for Your First Day The next step is preparing for your classes. We have all the info ready for you-everything from getting to class, to reviewing your schedule, and more. Access Your Lesley Email A Lesley email address has been assigned to you, and appears on your Enrollment Confirmation Letter. From this point forward, all university electronic communication will be sent to you at this address, so be sure to check your account frequently. Your password is the same one you’ve been using to check on the status of your documents during the admissions process. If you did not activate your account yet, you may do so now by visiting our password management site . Set Up Your Electronic Accounts Access your myLesley account This online course portal is where you can access class syllabi, assignments, online discussion boards, and library resources. Access your Self-Service account This is where you can find administrative information regarding your class schedules, grades, financial aid, and more. You will also use Self-Service to register for your courses. Connect With Your Advisor, Register for Classes, and Report Your Massachusetts Educator Licensure If you have any questions, you should reach out to your advisor. Their contact information can be found on your Enrollment Confirmation Letter. Or, you can reach out to us at grad.advising@lesley.edu for help. To register for courses, you should log in to your Self-Service account. All educator licensure candidates are required to report a MEPID to Lesley University. You will want to set up your electronic account with the Massachusetts Department of Elementary and Secondary Education (DESE) and submit your MEPID. ​​ Read more about setting up and submitting your MEPID. Educator Licensure and Certification The Certification and Licensure Office can help you with educator licensure, including becoming a licensed educator, renewing a teacher license, and transferring a license between states. MTEL (Massachusetts Tests for Educator Licensure) If you’re enrolled in an initial licensure program, you’ll be required to take and pass the MTEL during your studies. You’ll want to discuss your program’s MTEL policies with your assistant director of academic advising at the beginning of your program. ​​​ Read more about Massachusetts Educator Licensure. Obtain your ID card and purchase textbooks Lesley ID cards may be obtained at the Doble Public Safety Office at 34 Mellen Street in Cambridge, MA. ID cards are available 24 hours a day, 7 days a week. All textbooks are available at the Lesley University Bookstore . Your textbooks can also be delivered to your home or you can order them online to buy or rent on several websites. If purchasing a textbook is a hardship for you, please speak to your advisor and your professor to come up with a solution. You should purchase your textbook before classes start and no later than the end of the first day of classes. Review the Academic Calendar, Lesley Policies, and Learn How to Add/Drop Be sure to review the ​academic calendar so you’re aware of important dates and deadlines for registration, add/drop, and course terms. ​​ Find important information about university-wide policies and procedures , student services, and the history and culture of Lesley. If you need to add or drop a course, find the Add/Drop Withdrawal form you need via the Registrar's Office . Graduate Student Life & Housing Time in the classroom is just one part of the Lesley experience. We encourage you to explore our campus community, clubs and activities, and everything else we have to offer. ​Learn more about life at Lesley If you are interested in learning more about graduate housing options, please complete the interest form and a member of our graduate admissions team will be in touch. Take the next step Ready to begin your journey with Lesley? ​Share some basic information by filling out one of the forms below so that we can reach out to you with more information about our programs. Or, email admissions@lesley.edu to connect with a member of our admissions team. Undergraduate & Transfer: Inquiry Form Close | Visit | Apply Graduate: Inquiry Form Close | Visit | Apply Threshold Programs: Inquiry Form Close | Visit | Apply Lesley University Lesley University 29 Everett St, Cambridge, MA, 02138 617-868-9600 | Contact Lesley | Work at Lesley Instagram X LinkedIn Facebook YouTube Lesley is more than a university. We are an education and resource hub that educates and supports the world’s best practitioners in Education, Mental Health & Well-Being, Art & Design, Liberal Arts & Business. Lesley also educates neurodiverse learners through its innovative Threshold Programs. Learn more about Lesley ! Request Info Visit Apply Accessibility Privacy Policy Non-Discrimination Notice Accreditation © 2026 Lesley University"
    },
