Camões Scholars Understand the Cost of Attending Lesley Secure Your Funding and Pay Your Bill Student Financial Services Policies My Professional & Life Goals My Professional & Life Goals Reach My Professional & Life Goals Continuing Education Education Mental Health & Well-Being Art & Design Liberal Arts & Business Threshold Programs Professional Networks Priority Job Matching Program Alumni Engagement My Organization's Goals My Organization's Goals Reach My Organization's Goals Recruit Talent Become a Scholar Partner Priority Job Matching Program Retain Talent My Philanthropic Goals My Philanthropic Goals Reach My Philanthropic Goals Support Education at Lesley Support Mental Health & Well-Being Support Art & Design Support Liberal Arts & Business Support Threshold Campus Renovations and Future Vision Emerald Key Society Give Online Explore About Lesley About Lesley Explore About Lesley Leadership Faculty Strategic Framework Scholar Partner Program Fall Weekend 2026 Thought Leadership Series Work at Lesley Equity, Diversity, Inclusion, and Justice Updates from the President News & Stories Events Facility Rentals Contact Internal Internal Internal Academic Meetings and Selected Community Events 2026-2027 Brand Center Services Directory Support Hub Course Catalog myLesley Lesley Experience Portal Policies & Legal Academic Calendar Academic Catalog Institutional Review Board (IRB) MBTA Passes Veteran Benefits & Resources Accepted Students - Threshold You’re Right Where You Belong Congratulations, you’ve been accepted into the Threshold Programs at Lesley University! You’re about to begin a one-of-a-kind college experience built around your strengths, your goals, and your future. Now’s the time to get to know your new community, explore the campus you'll call home, and take the next steps toward independence and growth. We’re here to support you and your family every step of the way, so you feel excited, prepared, and ready to begin. Be sure to review these important resources for accepted students, and ​reach out to Colin Brady, Director of Threshold Admissions and Engagement if you have questions or need additional information. Commit to Lesley in Four Easy Steps We can't wait to have you join us at Lesley. But first, let's get you enrolled: Step 1: Username and password Find your Lesley username and password. Your username is at the bottom of your acceptance letter and your password is the same one you used to track your application in Self-Service . Step 2: Deposit If you've decided the Threshold Programs are right for you, please submit your enrollment deposit to secure your spot for Fall 2026. All spots in our incoming class are on a first-come, first-served basis. Log in to Lesley's Electronic Form System using your Lesley username, minus \"@lesley.edu.\" Submit your online enrollment contract and deposit . Step 3: Forms Complete the Housing Application and Vocational Questionnaire to complete your enrollment. You’ll also be required to complete your required health forms. Fall 2026 requirements will be posted shortly, however, you can ​​get a head start on forms for required immunizations . If you have any questions while completing these forms, feel free to contact us at cbrady5@lesley.edu or 857-360-5039. Step 4: New Student Orientation for Threshold Students We look forward to officially welcoming you as a member of the Lesley community! Please note : Orientation is mandatory for all new Threshold students. Should you have any questions about attending one of these events, please contact Colin Brady at cbrady5@lesley.edu . Register here Understand Your Financing Options We’re committed to making a Lesley education attainable and affordable. Our financial aid team will work with you and your family to help you understand what financial aid options are available,  and put together a plan that meets your needs. Learn more about cost & financial aid Questions? Contact Our Admissions Team If you have any questions as you work throughout the application process, please reach out to Colin Brady, Director of Threshold Admissions & Engagement , who can assist you and provide additional information. General phone and email: 857-360-5039 cbrady5@lesley.edu Take the next step Ready to begin your journey with Lesley? ​Share some basic information by filling out one of the forms below so that we can reach out to you with more information about our programs. Or, email admissions@lesley.edu to connect with a member of our admissions team. Undergraduate & Transfer: Inquiry Form Close | Visit | Apply Graduate: Inquiry Form Close | Visit | Apply Threshold Programs: Inquiry Form Close | Visit | Apply Lesley University Lesley University 29 Everett St, Cambridge, MA, 02138 617-868-9600 | Contact Lesley | Work at Lesley Instagram X LinkedIn Facebook YouTube Lesley is more than a university. We are an education and resource hub that educates and supports the world’s best practitioners in Education, Mental Health & Well-Being, Art & Design, Liberal Arts & Business. Lesley also educates neurodiverse learners through its innovative Threshold Programs. Learn more about Lesley ! Request Info Visit Apply Accessibility Privacy Policy Non-Discrimination Notice Accreditation © 2026 Lesley University"
    },
    "https://lesley.edu/my-professional-life-goals/priority-job-matching-program": {
      "title": "Priority Job Matching Program",
      "description": "Priority Job Matching Program | Lesley University Skip to main content Search Breadcrumb Home My Professional & Life Goals My Professional & Life Goals Priority Job Matching Program Main Reach My Education Goals My Education Goals Reach My Education Goals Education Programs Undergraduate Programs Master's Programs PhD Programs Certificate Programs Mental Health & Well Being Programs Undergraduate Programs Master's Programs Counseling & Psychology Expressive Therapies Social Work PhD Programs Certificate Programs Art & Design Programs Undergraduate Programs MFA in Visual and Literary Arts Liberal Arts & Business Programs Undergraduate Programs Graduate Programs Certificate Programs Threshold Programs Life at Lesley Housing Threshold Housing Clubs and Activities Athletics Dining International Student Services (ISS) International F-1 and Form I-20 International Student Housing International Student Forms Travel Information Understanding Your Immigration Documents Maintaining Legal F-1 Status Work Authorization Practical Tips for International Students Student Support Resources Avoid Scams and Frauds Join Admissions Undergraduate Students How to Apply Admissions Visits & Events Accepted Students Submit Your Deposit Graduate Students How to Apply Education Programs Mental Health & Well-Being Programs Art & Design Programs Liberal Arts & Business Admissions Visits & Events Accepted Students Submit Your Deposit Transfer Students How to Apply Admissions Visits & Events Accepted Students Submit Your Deposit Mass Guarantee Degree Completion Students How to Apply Admissions Visits & Events Accepted Students Submit Your Deposit International Students How to Apply Admissions Visits & Events Accepted Students Submit Your Deposit Threshold Students How to Apply Admissions Visits & Events Accepted Students Submit Your Deposit Meet the Admissions Team Costs & Financial Aid Options for Financing Your Education Private Scholarships Maine Scholars Program Urban Scholars Initiative Hometown Scholars Camões Scholars Understand the Cost of Attending Lesley Secure Your Funding and Pay Your Bill Student Financial Services Policies My Professional & Life Goals My Professional & Life Goals Reach My Professional & Life Goals Continuing Education Education Mental Health & Well-Being Art & Design Liberal Arts & Business Threshold Programs Professional Networks Priority Job Matching Program Alumni Engagement My Organization's Goals My Organization's Goals Reach My Organization's Goals Recruit Talent Become a Scholar Partner Priority Job Matching Program Retain Talent My Philanthropic Goals My Philanthropic Goals Reach My Philanthropic Goals Support Education at Lesley Support Mental Health & Well-Being Support Art & Design Support Liberal Arts & Business Support Threshold Campus Renovations and Future Vision Emerald Key Society Give Online Explore About Lesley About Lesley Explore About Lesley Leadership Faculty Strategic Framework Scholar Partner Program Fall Weekend 2026 Thought Leadership Series Work at Lesley Equity, Diversity, Inclusion, and Justice Updates from the President News & Stories Events Facility Rentals Contact Internal Internal Internal Academic Meetings and Selected Community Events 2026-2027 Brand Center Services Directory Support Hub Course Catalog myLesley Lesley Experience Portal Policies & Legal Academic Calendar Academic Catalog Institutional Review Board (IRB) MBTA Passes Veteran Benefits & Resources Priority Job Matching Program Connecting the best practitioners with world-class employers. Our job support resources help professionals at every stage of their careers find roles that align not only with the skills and strengths, but with the values and ideals that guide them. And they provide employers across our focus areas of education , mental health and well-being , art and design , liberal arts and business , and educating neurodiverse learners with access to Lesley’s highly respected alumni community and practitioner ecosystem. Career connections at Lesley extend far beyond the typical job board and include: Career Fairs Leveraging our deep partnerships with leading employers across our focus areas, we host targeted, industry specific job fairs that connect practitioners with open positions at a range of organizations. Using Lesley to find your next opportunity means cutting through the clutter, and getting connected directly with organizations who need talent. Alumni Connections We also support alumni by keeping their resumes on file and making them available to partner organizations to search. These curated connections help employers find the best, most highly qualified candidates, and give our alumni enhanced access to quality positions in their field. Join our extensive network of alumni and employers in education, mental health, arts, and more. By uploading your resume to our secure database, you'll be automatically matched with job opportunities that suit your skills and experience. Lesley’s Priority Job Matching Program Lesley's Priority Job Matching Program offers more than just a database of resumes for an organization to cull through on its own; it provides a personalized approach to connecting Lesley alumni with the roles and organizations that best align with their skills and strengths. Lesley deeply understands our candidates - we look beyond qualifications towards unique talents, passions, and professional goals, which translates into taking the work out of finding the perfect match. We actively curate connections by matching alumni with current job listings from our employer partners and facilitate meaningful introductions. This tailored process ensures employers access to highly qualified candidates who are genuinely suited to their needs, while our alumni gain direct access to exceptional opportunities in their field. It’s a win-win that leverages Lesley’s intimate knowledge of our community to foster lasting professional relationships. Want to be notified when this program becomes available? Keep me posted Lesley University Lesley University 29 Everett St, Cambridge, MA, 02138 617-868-9600 | Contact Lesley | Work at Lesley Instagram X LinkedIn Facebook YouTube Lesley is more than a university. We are an education and resource hub that educates and supports the world’s best practitioners in Education, Mental Health & Well-Being, Art & Design, Liberal Arts & Business. Lesley also educates neurodiverse learners through its innovative Threshold Programs. Learn more about Lesley ! Request Info Visit Apply Accessibility Privacy Policy Non-Discrimination Notice Accreditation © 2026 Lesley University"
    },
    "https://lesley.edu/my-organizations-goals/recruit-talent/priority-job-matching-program": {
      "title": "Priority Job Matching Program",
      "description": "Priority Job Matching Program | Lesley University Skip to main content Search Breadcrumb Home My Organization's Goals Recruit Talent Recruit Talent Priority Job Matching Program Main Reach My Education Goals My Education Goals Reach My Education Goals Education Programs Undergraduate Programs Master's Programs PhD Programs Certificate Programs Mental Health & Well Being Programs Undergraduate Programs Master's Programs Counseling & Psychology Expressive Therapies Social Work PhD Programs Certificate Programs Art & Design Programs Undergraduate Programs MFA in Visual and Literary Arts Liberal Arts & Business Programs Undergraduate Programs Graduate Programs Certificate Programs Threshold Programs Life at Lesley Housing Threshold Housing Clubs and Activities Athletics Dining International Student Services (ISS) International F-1 and Form I-20 International Student Housing International Student Forms Travel Information Understanding Your Immigration Documents Maintaining Legal F-1 Status Work Authorization Practical Tips for International Students Student Support Resources Avoid Scams and Frauds Join Admissions Undergraduate Students How to Apply Admissions Visits & Events Accepted Students Submit Your Deposit Graduate Students How to Apply Education Programs Mental Health & Well-Being Programs Art & Design Programs Liberal Arts & Business Admissions Visits & Events Accepted Students Submit Your Deposit Transfer Students How to Apply Admissions Visits & Events Accepted Students Submit Your Deposit Mass Guarantee Degree Completion Students How to Apply Admissions Visits & Events Accepted Students Submit Your Deposit International Students How to Apply Admissions Visits & Events Accepted Students Submit Your Deposit Threshold Students How to Apply Admissions Visits & Events Accepted Students Submit Your Deposit Meet the Admissions Team Costs & Financial Aid Options for Financing Your Education Private Scholarships Maine Scholars Program Urban Scholars Initiative Hometown Scholars Camões Scholars Understand the Cost of Attending Lesley Secure Your Funding and Pay Your Bill Student Financial Services Policies My Professional & Life Goals My Professional & Life Goals Reach My Professional & Life Goals Continuing Education Education Mental Health & Well-Being Art & Design Liberal Arts & Business Threshold Programs Professional Networks Priority Job Matching Program Alumni Engagement My Organization's Goals My Organization's Goals Reach My Organization's Goals Recruit Talent Become a Scholar Partner Priority Job Matching Program Retain Talent My Philanthropic Goals My Philanthropic Goals Reach My Philanthropic Goals Support Education at Lesley Support Mental Health & Well-Being Support Art & Design Support Liberal Arts & Business Support Threshold Campus Renovations and Future Vision Emerald Key Society Give Online Explore About Lesley About Lesley Explore About Lesley Leadership Faculty Strategic Framework Scholar Partner Program Fall Weekend 2026 Thought Leadership Series Work at Lesley Equity, Diversity, Inclusion, and Justice Updates from the President News & Stories Events Facility Rentals Contact Internal Internal Internal Academic Meetings and Selected Community Events 2026-2027 Brand Center Services Directory Support Hub Course Catalog myLesley Lesley Experience Portal Policies & Legal Academic Calendar Academic Catalog Institutional Review Board (IRB) MBTA Passes Veteran Benefits & Resources Priority Job Matching Program Connect with Qualified Talent Faster Finding motivated, qualified employees who understand your practice, share your values, and are prepared to make an impact on day one feels more challenging than ever. Posting jobs and sorting through endless resumes is time consuming and inefficient. But there is a better way. Our Priority Job Matching Program creates connections between organizations seeking talent and qualified Lesley alumni seeking roles in our core areas of education, mental health and well-being, art and design, liberal arts and business. It’s also for employers looking to create more inclusive, neurodiverse-friendly workplaces. When you partner with us, we’ll work to understand your specific needs, post your job listing, and then match you with skilled alumni actively seeking to connect with organizations that reflect their career values and aspirations. It’s a selective, curated network of Lesley-educated and -mentored prospective talent, which means a level of quality that you can trust. Lesley will help you find the right talent, so you can focus on the work that matters most. Ready to make hiring easier and better? Connect with our team to receive more information on our candidate pool and job matching process. Lesley University Lesley University 29 Everett St, Cambridge, MA, 02138 617-868-9600 | Contact Lesley | Work at Lesley Instagram X LinkedIn Facebook YouTube Lesley is more than a university. We are an education and resource hub that educates and supports the world’s best practitioners in Education, Mental Health & Well-Being, Art & Design, Liberal Arts & Business. Lesley also educates neurodiverse learners through its innovative Threshold Programs. Learn more about Lesley ! Request Info Visit Apply Accessibility Privacy Policy Non-Discrimination Notice Accreditation © 2026 Lesley University"
